Method Path Purpose Auth <code>GET</code> <code>/health</code> Liveness. <code>{"status":"ok"}</code> with no I/O. public <code>GET</code> <code>/install/status</code> <code>{"state":"installed"\|"not_installed"\|"partial","version":N\|null}</code> public <code>POST</code> <code>/install</code> Install the schema when <code>not_installed</code>. <code>409</code> once installed, <code>500</code> on <code>partial</code>. public <code>GET</code> <code>/diagnostics</code> Build version, schema state vs. expected, observability status. Never fails, even with the database down. any user <pre><code>// GET /v1/diagnostics
{
  "version": "3.1.0",
  "db_schema": { "state": "installed", "version": 3, "expected": 3 },
  "observability": { "enabled": true, "type": "http", "format": "ndjson" }
}
</code></pre>

Field Type Description <code>meta_tag</code> string · null Value of the <code>x-axium-meta-tag</code> request header. <code>tags</code> object (string → string) Every other <code>x-axium-&lt;name&gt;</code> request header, keyed by <code>&lt;name&gt;</code>. Repeated headers are dropped. <code>attributes</code> object Structured findings from policies. Today only <code>dlp_prompt</code>. <p><code>attributes.dlp_prompt</code>:</p> <pre><code>{
  "action": "none | keep | mask | block | error",
  "entities": [ { "entity": "IBAN", "kind": "financial", "country": "ES", "confirmed_by": "checksum" } ],
  "error": "optional message when action = error"
}
</code></pre> <p>Entity names and kinds only. The matched values are never recorded.</p>

envelope (default)ndjson <p>One JSON object per batch:</p> <pre><code>{
  "version": 1,
  "data": [
    { "trace_id": "…", "span_id": "…", "started_at": "…", "…": "…" },
    { "trace_id": "…", "span_id": "…", "started_at": "…", "…": "…" }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>Good for webhooks, serverless functions and any receiver that wants a single document per request.</p> <p>One JSON object per line, each line terminated by <code>\n</code>, no wrapper. The schema version travels only in the <code>x-axium-trace-version</code> header.</p> <pre><code>{"trace_id":"…","span_id":"…","started_at":"…", …}
{"trace_id":"…","span_id":"…","started_at":"…", …}
</code></pre> <p>Directly ingestible by ClickHouse (<code>FORMAT JSONEachRow</code>), BigQuery load jobs, Vector, Fluent Bit, Loki, Splunk HEC raw endpoints and most log pipelines.</p> <p>Every trace carries all 42 fields, always in the same order, with <code>null</code> where a value is unknown, <code>[]</code> for <code>policies_applied</code> and <code>{}</code> for <code>tags</code> and <code>attributes</code> when empty. The computed fields <code>latency_ms</code>, <code>tokens_total</code> and <code>cost</code> are not included; derive them at the receiver:</p> <pre><code>latency_ms   = ended_at - started_at           (milliseconds)
tokens_total = tokens_in + tokens_out          (null if either is null)
cost         = cost_in + cost_out              (null if either is null)
</code></pre> <p>Field definitions: Formats &amp; event schema.</p>

The container exits immediately with an environment error <p><code>envalid</code> prints the offending variable. Typical cases:</p> <ul> <li><code>MASTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY: must be 64 hex characters (32 bytes)</code>: a   trailing newline, a key of the wrong length, or a Base64 value. Generate   with <code>openssl rand -hex 32 | tr -d '\n'</code>.</li> <li><code>DATABASE_URL: ... missing</code>: not passed at all.</li> <li><code>AXIUM_METASERVER</code> or <code>PORT</code> invalid.</li> </ul> <code>[db] waiting for postgres...</code> for 30 seconds, then the process dies <p>The core cannot open a connection. Check, in order: the host in <code>DATABASE_URL</code> resolves from inside the container (<code>axium-db</code> on the same Docker network, not <code>localhost</code>), the port, the credentials, and that PostgreSQL accepts the connection (<code>pg_hba.conf</code>, Cloud SQL attachment, <code>sslmode</code>). A Cloud SQL DSN needs the <code>@localhost/db?host=/cloudsql/…</code> form.</p> <code>/v1/install/status</code> returns <code>not_installed</code> after startup <p>The automatic install failed. <code>grep '\[install\]'</code> in the logs. The usual message is <code>permission denied for database</code>: the user cannot create schemas.</p> <pre><code>GRANT CREATE ON DATABASE "axium-api" TO axium;
</code></pre> <p>Then restart the core, or call <code>POST /v1/install</code>.</p> <code>/v1/install/status</code> returns <code>partial</code> <p>Axium schemas exist without the <code>core.schema_version</code> table: an installation died halfway, or someone restored a partial dump. On a fresh installation, drop the schemas and restart:</p> <pre><code>DROP SCHEMA core, llm, rm, stats CASCADE;
</code></pre> <p>On a database with data, do not drop anything; contact support with the logs.</p> <code>The database is at schema version N but this build ships M</code> <p>You started an older image against a database that a newer version had already migrated. Deploy the newer image. Schema never downgrades.</p> <code>[install] migration failed</code> <p>The process exits on purpose. Restore the backup taken before the upgrade, roll the image back, and send the log line to support.</p> <code>[observability] disabled: …</code> <p>The destination could not be set up. Causes: unreadable DSN, the trace database user lacks <code>CREATE</code>, a <code>telemetry</code> schema left half-created (<code>partial</code>), an unparseable <code>OBSERVABILITY_HTTP_HEADERS</code>. Fix the value and restart; observability does not retry during the process's life.</p>
